    "---\n",
    "title: \"Title Tag Normalization Review\"\n",
    "subtitle: \"Deterministic normalization with conservative RapidFuzz candidates\"\n",
    "format:\n",
    "  html:\n",
    "    toc: true\n",
    "    code-fold: false\n",
    "    embed-resources: true\n",
    "jupyter: python3\n",
    "execute:\n",
    "  echo: true\n",
    "  warning: false\n",
    "params:\n",
    "  fuzzy_score_cutoff: 86\n",
    "  fuzzy_high_confidence_cutoff: 96\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Purpose\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook applies the selected starting workflow for turning free-form\n",
    "title tags into stable normalized labels. It does not update classification\n",
    "results or publish a normalization dictionary.\n",
    "\n",
    "The two stages are intentionally conservative:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. deterministic surface normalization;\n",
    "2. RapidFuzz lexical candidates for human review.\n",
    "\n",
    "Deterministic equivalences can be accepted automatically. RapidFuzz scores do\n",
    "not establish equivalence: numeric differences, compound tags, and broader\n",
    "families remain review decisions. Embeddings and BERTopic-style clustering are\n",
    "deferred until tags have descriptor types that prevent unrelated facets from\n",
    "being compared.\n",
    "\n",
    "The original tag remains the auditable source value. A future production layer\n",
    "should map it to a canonical tag and broader family rather than rewriting the\n",
    "stored model response.\n",
    "\n",
    "Render the offline deterministic and RapidFuzz baseline from the repository\n",
    "root:\n",
    "\n",
    "```bash\n",
    "QUARTO_PYTHON=.venv/bin/python quarto render \\\n",
    "  py_scripts/notebooks/model_tests/tag_normalization/tag_normalization_model_review.qmd\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
